# Executable semantic contract v1

Synthetic tasks are original; no historical dataset or sealed instrument is read.

## Causal tasks
`kind=causal`. `state` maps exactly x,y to integers (booleans are not integers). `rule` and `precondition` are ASTs. Every event is evaluated sequentially against current state. AST leaves `{var: event.status|event.amount|state.x|state.y}` or `{const: value}`. Constants and event status may be JSON scalar bool/int/string/null. Boolean nodes `{op: eq|ne|ge|gt|le|lt, args:[a,b]}`, `{op: all|any,args:[...]}`, `{op:not,args:[a]}`. Node shapes are exact; unknown variables/operators, wrong arities, and non-boolean rule/precondition roots are malformed. No coercion: equality is type-sensitive; ordered comparisons require operands of the same type, integer or string, excluding bool. `all`, `any`, and `not` require boolean operands. Empty `all` is true; empty `any` is false. Both gates are evaluated for every event; malformed AST branches are rejected even when another branch could short-circuit.
Events have `status`, positive integer `amount`, `op=add|scale|transfer|swap`, `source`, `destination`; x,y distinct for transfer/swap. Apply iff both rule and precondition evaluate true. Otherwise identity. add increments source; scale multiplies source; transfer subtracts amount from source and adds to destination (signed states allowed unless precondition forbids); swap exchanges simultaneous source/destination values. Output `{after: state, steps:[{cmp:{rule: bool,precondition:bool},calc:{operation: event.op or identity},after:state}]}`.

## Graph tasks
`kind=graph`. `nodes` distinct strings, `edges` triples [from,to,positive integer fuel cost], at most one edge per ordered pair. `start`, `goal`, `fuel`, `plan` list of destination names. Begin `{node:start,fuel:fuel}`. A move is legal iff edge exists and enough fuel; subtract edge cost. Stop immediately at first illegal action, state unchanged, subsequent actions are not evaluated. Output `{steps:[{legal:bool,after:state}], after:state, valid:bool, reaches_goal:bool, shortest_plan:list|null}`. Shortest plan minimizes moves within initial fuel, ties broken lexicographically by full destination sequence. Empty plan is legal. Reaches_goal requires entire proposed plan valid and terminal node equals goal.

## Block tasks
`kind=blocks`. `on` maps each block to another block or `TABLE`, with no cycles and at most one block directly on each block. Block names are distinct strings; `TABLE` is reserved. `goal_on` is a partial goal map referring only to existing blocks or `TABLE`; self-support, cycles, or multiple blocks assigned directly to one block are contradictory goals and malformed. Initial states with unknown supports, self-support, cycles, or multiple blocks directly on one block are malformed. `plan` list `{block,to}`. Move legal iff block exists and is clear, destination TABLE or existing clear block distinct from block, and destination differs from current support. On failure stop and retain state. Output same keys as graph except state is on-map. Shortest plan minimizes moves, ties by sequence of (block,to) ordered lexicographically.

## Critic tasks
`kind=critic`. `world` graph task (ignore its plan), `candidates` list `{candidate_id,plan,claimed_after}`. Candidate IDs are distinct strings; claimed state has exactly a world-node string and a nonnegative integer fuel. Each candidate independently starts at initial world state. `evaluations` contain candidate_id,valid,claim_correct,reaches_goal,remaining_moves,progress,usefulness,first_error,repair_plan. remaining_moves is minimum feasible remaining moves from executed final state; null when unreachable. progress = initial remaining moves minus final remaining moves for valid candidates with finite initial and final distances, else null. usefulness = -1 if invalid, 2 if valid and reaches goal, 1 if valid reachable and progress>0, 0 otherwise. first_error is first illegal step zero-based or `claim` if legal but wrong claimed final state, else null. repair_plan is optimal fresh plan from initial state (minimal-move replacement, not edit distance). Rank candidates by (valid and claim_correct, reaches_goal, usefulness, -remaining_moves, -len(plan)), descending; null distance treated worse than every finite one; exact ties returned as groups with IDs lexicographically sorted. target `{evaluations,ranking}`; validity and claim correctness are separate from progress and usefulness.

## Rendering and splits
Prompts contain entire contract relevant to task and JSON payload. Internal IDs/provenance/difficulty/splits/reviews are excluded. Twins and renderings share one family split assigned before rendering. Development challenges are exposed development data, never sealed evaluations. All answer-only/trace counterparts share split.
